{"availability":"available","full":"PicoPlus-devel/pico-infonesPlus","name":"pico-infonesPlus","description":"NES Emulator with SD card and menu support for the Raspberry PI Pico, Pico 2 and other RP2040/RP2350  based microcontrollers. Play your games from SD card on a HDMI display.","category":"Other","language":"C++","stars":532,"forks":55,"created":"2022-10-31T19:37:38Z","updated":"2026-10-08T11:14:09Z","license":"GPL-3.0","branch":"main","homepage":"","topics":["adafruit","adafruit-feather-dvi","emulator","hdmi","nes","nintendo-nes","pico","pimoroni","pimoroni-pico-dv","raspberry","raspberry-pi-pico","raspberry-pi-pico-2","rp2040","rp2350","sdcard","waveshare","waveshare-rp2040-pizero"],"demo":"https://shop.pimoroni.com/products/pimoroni-pico-dv-demo-base?variant=39494203998291","color":"#193546","ink":"#a6d6e8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T03:37:25.491Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-09T03:37:25.491Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-09T03:37:25.491Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-09T03:37:25.491Z","stars":532,"forks":55}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["pico-infonesPlus is a NES (Nintendo Entertainment System) emulator for Raspberry Pi Pico, Pico 2, and other RP2040/RP2350-based microcontrollers. It provides NES emulation with SD card support, an integrated menu system, and HDMI video output, enabling users to build compact, affordable retro gaming systems.","The emulator supports two player games using two NES controllers, two USB gamepads connected via a USB hub, or a USB gamepad combined with a NES controller.","When using a USB hub with a Raspberry Pi Pico, you need an OTG USB-Y cable to connect both power and the hub. On the Adafruit Fruit Jam, two USB gamepads can be connected directly to the two USB ports without a hub."],"features":["NES Emulation – Execute NES ROM files directly from an SD card","SD Card Menu System – Browse and launch games from an on-screen menu interface","Recently Played List – The last 20 games you started, one button press away in the menu (details)","USB Drive Mode – Present the SD card to a computer as a USB drive from the settings menu, so games can be added or removed without taking the card out (details)","Dual Controller Support – Two simultaneous controllers for multiplayer gameplay (details)"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/PicoPlus-devel/pico-infonesPlus/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"b6e0b4eb2eaa27168d210c1c1c9fb8e172cd092928c25bd6cb9cdca07c6229cb","extractedAt":"2026-10-09T03:37:25.633Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T03:37:25.633Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"pico-infonesPlus is a NES (Nintendo Entertainment System) emulator for Raspberry Pi Pico, Pico 2, and other RP2040/RP2350-based microcontrollers. It provides NES emulation with SD card support, an integrated menu system, and HDMI video output, enabling users to build compact, affordable retro gaming systems.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/PicoPlus-devel/pico-infonesPlus/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"b6e0b4eb2eaa27168d210c1c1c9fb8e172cd092928c25bd6cb9cdca07c6229cb","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/PicoPlus-devel/pico-infonesPlus/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-09T03:37:25.635Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-10-08T11:14:09Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/PicoPlus-devel/pico-infonesPlus/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-09T03:37:25.640Z","hash":"b6e0b4eb2eaa27168d210c1c1c9fb8e172cd092928c25bd6cb9cdca07c6229cb","originalBytes":105526,"storedBytes":105526,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["controller","nes","usb","pico","port","game","board","when","adafruit","connect","two","player","using","card","controllers","menu","note","only","games","rp2350","boards","emulator","pcb","wii","classic","hdmi","start","flash","breakout","image","see","audio","psram","select","button","power","waveshare","file","build","micro","settings","breadboard","cable","one","raspberry","rp20